[tool_result]1	# Virtual Battery Factory 2	 3	An LLM-agent-driven, cross-scale virtual battery design platform: a fully 4	software-simulated closed loop spanning material design, cell design, and 5	safety assessment --- with no dependence on physical experiments. 6	 7	The agent executes a **protocolized governance** design loop (five-stage 8	multi-precision funnel, evaluation-and-fallback routing, mechanized 9	adjudication with an evidence-chain audit ledger) specified entirely in 10	natural language. The protocol itself is a self-contained declarative 11	artifact (`.claude/skills/virtual-battery-factory/`) and is 12	harness-independent by construction --- cross-harness portability runs under 13	the OpenAI Agents SDK and LangChain live in `paper/portability/`. 14	 15	## Entry point and structure 16	 17	- **`run.py`** (repo root): a thin Agent SDK launcher. It loads the protocol 18	  skill (`.claude/skills/virtual-battery-factory/SKILL.md`) verbatim into the 19	  agent's system prompt and drives the simulation library `python -m bda` 20	  through the harness's built-in shell tool. No custom tools are registered. 21	- The protocol skill is self-contained under 22	  `.claude/skills/virtual-battery-factory/`: `SKILL.md` (the protocol), 23	  `references/cli-commands.md` (command reference), 24	  `scripts/bda/` (the simulation library, pip-editable install), and 25	  `assets/` (sample cases). If the environment is missing, the agent 26	  installs it itself per protocol step 0. 27	- **Cross-harness legs** (portability experiment, §4.6 of the paper): 28	  `paper/portability/oa_sdk/run_oa.py` (OpenAI Agents SDK --- protocol 29	  injected as instructions) and `paper/portability/langchain/run_lc.py` 30	  (LangChain --- protocol loaded via an on-demand `load_skill` tool), with 31	  batch drivers `run_oa_matrix.py` / `run_lc_matrix.py`. 32	 33	## Installation 34	 35	```powershell 36	python -m venv .venv 37	.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1 38	pip install -e ".claude/skills/virtual-battery-factory/scripts[dev,ml,host]" 39	``` 40	 41	External binaries (needed only for the closing true-compute endorsement; 42	each runner locates the executable via `PATH`): 43	 44	| Binary | Purpose | Source | 45	|---|---|---| 46	| xtb | Semi-empirical quantum single points (funnel pre-screen) | [github.com/grimme-lab/xtb/releases](https://github.com/grimme-lab/xtb/releases) | 47	| ORCA | True DFT endorsement (Top-3) | [faccts.de/orca](https://www.faccts.de/orca/) (academic license) | 48	| GROMACS | True MD endorsement (Top-1) | [gromacs.org/Downloads](https://www.gromacs.org/Downloads) | 49	 50	ML potentials (MACE-MP/CHGNet) ship with the `[ml]` extra. Cases with 51	`real_compute: false` need none of the above. 52	 53	### Environment bootstrap (no secrets on disk) 54	 55	Create `.env` in the repo root before running: 56	`DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=<your key>`. `run.py` resolves configuration in order 57	(existing environment variables always win): 58	 59	| Variable | Default | Meaning | 60	|---|---|---| 61	| `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` | `https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic` | Anthropic-compatible endpoint | 62	| `ANTHROPIC_MODEL` | `deepseek-v4-pro` | Model name | 63	| `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` | `.env`'s `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` | Credential; skipped if an Anthropic token is already set | 64	 65	Secrets are injected only into child-process environment variables, never 66	written to files, never printed. Connectivity smoke test: 67	`.venv\Scripts\python.exe run.py --smoke-test`. 68	 69	## Running 70	 71	**The user's only input is natural language** --- no YAML is ever written or 72	read by hand. State the design objective directly (e.g., "design a battery 73	with energy density ≥ 400 Wh/kg and 4C fast charge without lithium 74	plating"): 75	 76	1. The skill clarifies item by item via AskUserQuestion (objective 77	   quantification / starting stage / system / ablation / true-compute 78	   switch --- all with defaults). 79	2. After clarification the skill records the criteria, writes them into